            <ArticleTitle>Medical assessment after injury--problems encountered: IV. Backache.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>225-34</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Most of us have had backache at some time in our lives and it may be very difficult to sort out the complaint of backache after an injury. However a systematic approach together with an assessment of the injured person's reaction to his injuries will generally help. A working structured approach is given together with special tests where exaggeration is suspected. Reference is made to the percentage assessment of backache following injury. Finally it is stressed that &quot;Prophylaxis is the best treatment&quot; especially in an industrial setting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
